# 12-Bar Blues Shuffle in A (repertoire plan: st-blues-shuffle-a). An original study on the
# traditional 12-bar form: A A A A | D D A A | E D A E, played twice, then the last A.
# Swung eighths are written as triplets: a long note (q3, two thirds of the beat) and a short one
# (e3, the last third). The shuffle figure is a root with its fifth, then with its sixth.
title: 12-Bar Blues Shuffle in A
